  "interpretation": "Passing establishes only static agreement on the 128-case, 8-by-16, source-grounded direct-accumulation protocol: K=4 uses a predeclared four-way exact visible-input fork; the teacher is scheduled by novel-cluster/support-milestone fingerprints from current and cumulative source evidence without filtering by the next block's case mix; and hard trust gates directly admit safe, source-grounded documents to the working library. The next unseen block compares the new document increment with its exact parent before any teacher call. F/Q, practical safety, exposure, and uncertainty are reported as a prequential learning diagnostic and teacher direction; a single block never rolls back the working library or excludes that block from teacher evidence. A domain document may be nominated from one exact causal source case; a general document still requires two source domains. B8 additionally freezes comparison arms before its increment diagnostic; performance nonpass is reported, while only intervention-isolation failure blocks the accumulated-library freeze. The training-run CN30 entry is only a two-arm Ours-versus-empty mechanism diagnostic. The paper main table instead requires one four-arm controller, one method-independent fixed route artifact, and an immutable external-ready Ours training-source binding made before any CN30 adapter, route, or model call (byte-hash verification remains separately disclosed). Historical method-level CN30 aggregates have already been observed for protocol diagnosis, so a later locked CN30 run is benchmark-aware rather than a pristine confirmatory test; CN30 cases and outcomes remain excluded from the training lawyer and Luna teacher. Passing is not evidence of runtime qualification, learned improvement, or benchmark performance."
